          "guid": "mt4yko9k031l0nnz",
          "message": {
            "text": "Capture has already applied Blink's form-specific color serialization: legacy alpha uses CSSOM's two/three-decimal 8-bit form, while modern color() alpha uses six-decimal StringBuilder precision. The shared RGBA representation erases that lexical provenance, so colorAlphaStr preserves the union at up to six decimals rather than re-quantizing; SVG coordinate format.r remains unchanged.",
            "markdown": "Capture has already applied Blink's form-specific color serialization: legacy alpha uses CSSOM's two/three-decimal 8-bit form, while modern color() alpha uses six-decimal StringBuilder precision. The shared RGBA representation erases that lexical provenance, so colorAlphaStr preserves the union at up to six decimals rather than re-quantizing; SVG coordinate format.r remains unchanged."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/render/colors.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 89,
                  "endLine": 106,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "/**\n * Preserve the precision of captured CSS alpha without applying SVG coordinate\n * rounding.\n *\n * Capture has already applied Blink's form-specific serialization: legacy\n * colors use the CSSOM 8-bit two/three-decimal rule, while modern `color()`\n * alpha uses StringBuilder's six-decimal precision (Chromium 7d859f27,\n * `Color::SerializeLegacyColorAsCSSColor` / `Color::SerializeInternal`). This\n * shared RGBA representation no longer carries that lexical provenance, so\n * retaining up to the source maximum is the only lossless common route.\n */\nfunction colorAlphaStr(alpha: number): string {\n  const clamped = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, alpha));\n  return Number(clamped.toFixed(6)).toString();\n}\n\nexport function colorStr(c: RGBA): string {\n  return c.a < 1 ? `rgba(${c.r},${c.g},${c.b},${colorAlphaStr(c.a)})` : `rgb(${c.r},${c.g},${c.b})`;"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
